From 90b9e166b65caececaabae5e9bc16da5b59924b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:44:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/32] feat(gemm): sm120gemv BF16 backend, Triton skinny GEMM
 for M<=32 on SM12x

--bf16-gemm-backend sm120gemv routes BF16 linears with M<=32, K%128==0,
N<=65536 to a weight-streaming Triton kernel (W@X^T on mma.sync, evict-first
weights, in-kernel deterministic split-K via per-tile tickets, per-stream
workspace, CUDA-graph safe). Everything else stays on cuBLAS.
GPU2 (sm_120) vs cuBLAS, cold weights, graph replay: 1.00-1.25x across the
qwen38-flash-next dense shapes at M=1..32; correctness vs fp32 matches cuBLAS.
